    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80fa854d_cfba369d",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/generic/pdc_power_mgmt_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1559,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-14T22:16:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had hoped to remove the wait-for-idle hook into the subsystem and do any test/subsystem synchronization through the emulator. I\u0027d prefer not to add another test hook into the subsystem. The cycles of the power management state machine are not part of its public interface, and I don\u0027t want to write tests in terms of them.\n\nI would have thought that this wouldn\u0027t be necessary, though. Shouldn\u0027t `board_set_active_charge_port` send an event to the subsystem? If not, how does the subsystem start sinking power after the active charge port changes?",
      "parentUuid": "caaabe4c_67e5a7b3",
      "revId": "9057975496c61b4402cc0cefa763290a9a21ec7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "952d7b37_047f6277",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/generic/pdc_power_mgmt_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1559,
      "author": {
        "id": 1547258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-15T04:00:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As soon as board_set_active_charge_port is called, the state machine should transit to SNK_ATTACHED_SET_SINK_PATH state to send CMD_PDC_SET_SINK_PATH to PDC, the delay is dependent on LOOP_DELAY_MS in pdc thread.\n\nWhen board_set_active_charge_port is called before entering SNK_ATTACHED_RUN state, the sink path configuration is handled by the state machine. When board_set_active_charge_port is called in SNK_ATTACHED_RUN state, the test code can either sleep for LOOP_DELAY_MS ms or send PDC_SM_EVENT to run the state machine.\n\nI came up with two options:\n1. Call board_set_active_charge_port in test code in SNK_ATTACHED_RUN state, put the test code to sleep for (LOOP_DELAY_MS + 1) ms to let the state machine run. The advantage is the code in pdc_power_mgmt.c is not touched.\n1. In pdc_power_mgmt_set_active_charge_port, post PDC_SM_EVENT if the state in SNK_ATTACHED_RUN. The advantage is faster response for board_set_active_charge_port.",
      "parentUuid": "80fa854d_cfba369d",
      "revId": "9057975496c61b4402cc0cefa763290a9a21ec7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "920837ca_230b9aa0",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/generic/pdc_power_mgmt_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1559,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T21:29:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If those are the two options, my strong preference would be for option 1. The wait times in `native_sim` are made-up, i.e. waiting longer doesn\u0027t actually take more wall clock or CPU time. There\u0027s no advantage to having something happen \"faster.\" There is an advantage to not adding test hooks to `pdc_power_mgmt.c`.\n\nI think the ultimate solution to problems like this is to properly implement wait-for-idle in the emulators. Right now, it\u0027s the drivers waiting until no commands are active, which is another inappropriate test hook. It should really be the emulators waiting until no commands have been in flight for X ms. If that existed, you could use it here to know when `pdc_power_mgmt` was done reacting to `set_active_charge_port`.",
      "parentUuid": "952d7b37_047f6277",
      "revId": "9057975496c61b4402cc0cefa763290a9a21ec7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
